## FOUND

I attacked the repairs, not the findings — as instructed. **The pattern held for a third round: two of this candidate's own prior repairs are the direct cause of the P1 I found.**

### V63-D3 — P1 — a mutation request the model does not classify derives **no intent**, and the fabrication ships

With the model emitting no `requestIntent` (the tier the request lexicon exists to backstop), **18 of 18** ordinary mutation requests I wrote derive `requestedIntent === null`. §3 rule 3 never fires. Measured through the **real** intent window *and* the **real** structured-claim window: **18/18 fabricated completions reached the founder-facing summary verbatim**, `receiptRendered: false`. **0 false positives** on my read controls; all positive controls still work.

| Class | Example | Mechanism |
|---|---|---|
| **(a)** compound "mutate **then** report" | `archive ACME then tell me` | `alwaysInImperativePosition=true`, `lexiconImperative="archive"` — the imperative **is** recognised — then vetoed because `lastClauseIsRead`. `lastClauseIsMutation` exists; **there is no `firstClauseIsMutation`.** |
| **(b)** adverb before the imperative | `quickly archive ACME`, `permanently delete …` | `REQUEST_FRAME_PREFIX` is a closed list with no adverb slot |
| **(c)** email object | `invite dorj@example.com as engineer` | `IMPERATIVE_OBJECT` doesn't accept an email — the whole invite family is invisible |
| **(d)** object noun = finite verb | `create a work order …`, `delete the cost model` | `STATEMENT_FINITE_VERB` contains `works?`, `ends?`, `costs?` |
| **(e)** confirmation | `ok go` | bare `go` is not in the follower set |
| **(f)** **Mongolian polite imperative** | `ACME-г архивлана уу`, `Зенит-г сэргээнэ үү` | `MN_READ_SHAPE` reads **every** sentence-final `уу/үү` as a question. The stem **is** matched (`alwaysCyrillicRaw="архивлана"`) and then discarded. |

**(a) is the V59-D2 repair applied in exactly one of the two tiers that need it** — `commandReadLeadEffective` fixed this class for the company command-fallback and was never carried into the request-intent tier the receipt rule depends on. **(f) was introduced by the V61-D6 repair.** A discriminator exists and is as general as the rule it would join: a finite non-past `-на/-нэ/-но/-нө` before `уу/үү` is a polite imperative; a participle (`-сан/-сэн`) or infinitive (`-х`) is a question.

**v92 measurement (regression vs parity, stated separately):** of the 20 fabrications, v92's PCCP corrects **1**. **19/20 v92 PARITY, 1/20 truth REGRESSION.** Under the contract bar all 20 violate §3 rule 3 — and the founder's stated bar for this round is explicit that a false negative letting a fabrication ship is a **P1**.

### Also found

- **V63-D2 (P2)** — `archivedCompanyIds`, the gate that **refuses** new work under an archived company, reads the raw trimmed arrays while `contextCompanyIds`, the gate that **trusts**, is trim-proof. After a floor pass the id is trusted and no longer known-archived → a create lands under an archived parent. **The asymmetry runs in the unsafe direction.** Reachable at ~17–18k-char commands **on turns that still answer**. Executably demonstrated.
- **V63-D1 (P2)** — `memories` and `factoryWorkOrders` cannot express their own trim (`total:null, truncated:null`). **V62-D4 is not closed**: the claimed `count:exact` is absent on the primary paths (`match_memories` RPC; the non-factory `canonical_work_orders` query) and discarded by the envelope literals anyway. Their `scope` strings become false. **This is the one working construction for "a trim answers a count from a window".**
- **V63-D4 (P2)** — **6 of 19 mutants survive the whole 57-suite battery.** Three are the last two rounds' own P1 fixes: the id-provenance capture (V62-D1), the image gate (V62-D2 — pinned by a substring a `false &&` leaves intact), and the min-safe assertion. Also: the org sentinel can become `status !== 'archived'` (a company under an archived **parent** then reports active) and nothing notices.
- **V63-D6 (P2)** — a **malformed** (not absent) `SEM_AI_MAX_TOKENS` → `NaN` → the trim empties the whole optional pack **every turn**, `overBudget:false`, no error. All three caps share it; the incident record itself invites the founder to edit that variable.
- **V63-D5 / D7 / D8 (P3)** — the min-safe assertion is vacuous (V61-D4 open); the platform request-body limit is an unnamed whole-request gate (the hidden fifth); the pinned witness claims a 12,340 calibration but measures 25,595.

## ROOT CAUSE

A repair made in one tier and not its twin (V63-D3a), a general language rule that swallowed the command form it was meant to leave alone (V63-D3f), and — three times — a P1 fix pinned by the **presence of a substring** rather than by behaviour, so the next round's edit can silently undo it (V63-D4).

## SYSTEMIC IMPACT

The never-silent receipt is only as good as intent detection, and intent detection has no behavioural safety net when the model stays quiet. The trim now protects *trust* everywhere and *refusal* nowhere.

